IMP:

All reverse proxies can act as Load balancer but not vice versa. It depends on the configuration
of the LB.

Type 1:
LB configured with SNAT(L7)
this will terminate the existing connection and create a new connection with its
own ip to the backend-> hence acts as rev proxy
Ex: Nginx

LB confiured as by pass (L4/DSR)
just routes the traffic to the backend without altrering ip -> hence not rev proxy
Ex: Azure SLB
But Azure App Gateway -> acts as reverse proxy.

